# query-svc's own database — independent of packages/db's (the verifier's own RDS instance).
# Same variable NAMES as packages/db/.env.example on purpose: @scvs/db's readDbEnv() is re-exported
# unchanged (see src/index.ts) and reads these bare names with no per-package prefix. What makes this
# package's database independent is which VALUES a deployed environment's Terraform binds into
# query-svc's own task definition (config/env-manifest.yaml's `query-postgres` group), not a
# different variable shape.
#
# Locally there is only one docker-compose Postgres (docker/docker-compose.yml) and one root .env, so
# in local dev packages/db and packages/db-query point at the SAME local database by default — that
# is harmless in dev (no instance-separation stakes locally) and is not the thing this split protects
# against. Override POSTGRES_DB here (or export DATABASE_URL) if you want a second local database to
# mirror the deployed separation more closely.
POSTGRES_HOST="localhost"
POSTGRES_PORT="5433"
POSTGRES_DB="scvs"
POSTGRES_USER="scvs"
POSTGRES_PASSWORD="scvs_local_dev"
# POSTGRES_SSL="true"  # set to "true" against RDS (rds.force_ssl=1); local docker-compose Postgres doesn't terminate TLS
